    "result_text": "Patrons now carry shares and backing is weighted by them. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**The change** is in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`, the only place the patrons cell and backing were computed:\n- **Shares:** each patron gets 100.00 divided by the number of patrons, rounded half to even to two decimals. The first-named patron also gets whatever is left over to make 100.00. With three patrons that's 33.34, 33.33, 33.33.\n- **Patrons cell:** shows `<name> <share>`, sorted by name, e.g. `Ben 33.34, Cam 33.33, Dot 33.33`.\n- **Backing:** each patron's settled figure from the last 90 days, times their share divided by 100. I add these up exactly and round half to even once at the end. The request could also be read as rounding each patron's amount separately, which can differ by a cent; the tests pass either way.\n\nI didn't add a database table or column for shares. The server already returns patrons in the order they were named, so the shares can always be worked out from that order. Storing them would only be needed if shares could later be set by hand.\n\n**A separate bug I fixed:** one scenario failed in the \"as of\" past-date view, for a reason unrelated to patrons. When person aliases were added, their table was never included in the past-sheet rebuild list in `SheetPasts.java`. So once a merge had given someone an alias, rebuilding the sheet for a past date crashed with a database error and the past view showed no rows. I added the alias table to that list. Two other tables are also missing from it, holidays and claim templates. They don't cause a crash, but past views currently show today's holidays and templates. I left those alone because the tests don't cover them.",
